<div class="fm-care-root" data-testid="content-page-rug-care-selection-guide">
  <!-- Header Banner -->
  <header class="fm-care-header">
    <div class="fm-care-header-inner">
      <span class="fm-care-eyebrow">Guide</span>
      <h1 class="fm-care-title">Rug Care & Selection Guide</h1>
      <p class="fm-care-subtitle">Everything you need to look after your rug — and choose the right size for your room.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="fm-care-body-sec">
    <div class="fm-care-body-inner">

      <!-- 1. General care -->
      <h2 class="fm-care-h2">General care</h2>
      <ul class="fm-care-ul">
        <li><strong>Sunlight:</strong> Limit continuous and direct exposure to sunlight.</li>
        <li><strong>Rotation:</strong> Rotate your rug periodically for even wear.</li>
        <li><strong>Loose threads:</strong> Trim loose threads carefully with scissors — never pull.</li>
        <li><strong>Furniture protectors:</strong> Use protectors under heavy furniture legs to prevent pile from flattening.</li>
        <li><strong>Shedding:</strong> Expect natural shedding for the first few months, up to about six. It reduces over time.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional cleaning:</strong> Have your rug professionally cleaned every 2–3 years by trusted experts. Ask for a pre-cleaning inspection and a written receipt with a work guarantee.</li>
        <li><strong>Spills:</strong> Address spills immediately by blotting with a clean, absorbent cloth. Rinse and dry thoroughly to prevent staining.</li>
        <li><strong>Ventilation:</strong> To freshen a rug, turn it upside down and beat it gently in an open space to remove loose yarn and dust.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 2. Vacuuming -->
      <h2 class="fm-care-h2">Vacuuming</h2>
      <p class="fm-care-p">Vacuum regularly to remove surface dirt and prevent discoloration.</p>
      <ul class="fm-care-ul">
        <li>Use a low-power setting and avoid a beater brush.</li>
        <li>Canister vacuums, brooms, and hand-held attachments are best.</li>
        <li>Strong-suction vacuums can pull fibres from the base — not recommended.</li>
        <li>Avoid repeated vacuuming across edges and fringes to prevent damage.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 3. Storing rugs safely -->
      <h2 class="fm-care-h2">Storing rugs safely</h2>
      <ul class="fm-care-ul">
        <li><strong>Wrap:</strong> Before storing, wrap the rug in plastic or fabric.</li>
        <li><strong>Roll, don't fold:</strong> Roll the rug with the front side facing outwards, then cover with cloth.</li>
        <li><strong>Environment:</strong> Keep the rolled rug in a dry area with good air circulation; clean the space regularly to deter pests.</li>
        <li><strong>Don't pile items on it:</strong> Weight on a stored rug can damage the pile permanently.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 4. Sizing — how to pick the right rug -->
      <h2 class="fm-care-h2">Sizing — how to pick the right rug</h2>
      <ul class="fm-care-ul">
        <li><strong>Measure first:</strong> Note your room's dimensions and any limitations like doorways.</li>
        <li><strong>Go a size larger:</strong> A larger rug tends to unify a room and make it feel more cohesive.</li>
        <li><strong>The 18-inch rule:</strong> Aim for roughly 18 inches of exposed floor around the perimeter — adjust based on room size and layout.</li>
        <li><strong>Trust your eye:</strong> These are guidelines. Experiment until it feels right.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 5. Measuring an abstract-shaped rug -->
      <h3 class="fm-care-h3">Measuring an abstract-shaped rug</h3>
      <ul class="fm-care-ul">
        <li><strong>Consider the useable area:</strong> Irregular shapes may not cover the floor uniformly — plan for how it will actually sit.</li>
        <li><strong>Outline the area:</strong> Use painter's tape to mark the area you want covered; it helps you visualise footprint and flow.</li>
        <li><strong>Measure length and width:</strong> Within the outlined space, take the maximum length and width to arrive at the largest possible dimensions.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 6. How to measure the rug itself -->
      <h3 class="fm-care-h3">How to measure the rug itself</h3>
      <ul class="fm-care-ul">
        <li>Stretch the tape from the longest point to the opposite end for maximum length.</li>
        <li>Repeat at the widest part for the width. The two measurements may not be directly opposite each other.</li>
        <li>Think about how the shape complements or contrasts with existing furniture in the room.</li>
      </ul>

    </div>
  </section>
</div>
